| A string concatenates with any scalar, but not with an object: an object
| has no bare form to splice in, so `Str + Object` stays a type error (the
| same reason `{a = 1} + 3` is one). One array operand is different — the
| array rule makes the string an element — so only the object case fails.
let x = "config: " + { port = 8080 }
